{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"slowmoving-engaging-kouprey","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nS1 proves one atomic update executor and S2 produces pure plans, but legacy batch dispatch still replays compound methods, conflates deferred and applied work, and uses a rolling breaker that cannot distinguish physical attempts from exhausted logical outcomes. One ticket-local or permanent failure can distort batch behavior.\n\n## Outcome\nMake the typed coordinator authoritative for non-create plans: update, delete, probe, clean-label, repair-property, and conflict handling. Execute atomic desired postconditions in dependency order; after partial success, re-observe and plan only remaining drift. Produce exact ticket/pass outcomes and apply the approved endpoint/provider finite-pass fuse only to normalized exhausted logical failures.\n\n## Plan\n1. Add a coordinator that consumes immutable plans, enforces dependencies, and calls adapter atomic operations through S1s budget. Preserve successful earlier postconditions and never replay the whole compound mutation after a late failure.\n2. Normalize auto-healed, success, deferred, permanent, commit-unknown, exhausted transient, and skipped dispositions with ticket/endpoint/tenant/provider/global scope.\n3. Replace the rolling 5-of-10 breaker. Endpoint scope opens after three consecutive eligible exhausted logical outcomes across at least two tickets; provider scope additionally spans two endpoint families. A matching success resets consecutive state.\n4. Exclude physical attempts, recovered warnings, permanent failures, ticket-local 404, and opaque diagnostics from inferred fuse counters. Retain direct authoritative credential, configuration, quota, rate, issue, endpoint, tenant, and global behavior.\n5. When a fuse opens, defer remaining matching plans with reason/scope/retry metadata while independent scopes continue. Preserve exact applied/failed/deferred/skipped tallies and nonzero degraded-pass signaling.\n\n## Testing (RED → GREEN)\n- Coordinator tables cover dependency success/failure, partial compound update, idempotent already-gone delete, ticket-local 404 isolation, permanent 4xx, auth/quota/rate scopes, and mixed endpoint families.\n- Fuse sequences assert threshold, two-ticket/two-family requirements, success reset, exclusions, and independent-scope continuation.\n- Replay fixtures derived from historical GitHub Actions outcomes assert zero premature stop in the completed 1,200-run slice; raw warning/grep text is never classified as a terminal outcome.\n- Verified-fake Cloud/DC batches assert wire order, maximum calls, exact tallies, logs, and exit status.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nCut over by non-create operation family and never dual-send. Before legacy removal, an operation-family flag can select the old dispatcher. Rollback preserves successful Jira effects and resumes from re-observation. The intentional differences are three-call shared budgeting, explicit deferral, exact partial outcomes, and replacement of the rolling breaker.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Non-create plans execute atomic postconditions once in dependency order; a late failure preserves earlier success and re-observes only remaining drift within the same logical budget.\n- [ ] Ticket-local/permanent failures isolate the ticket, authoritative broad scopes stop only their declared scope, and independent tickets/endpoints continue.\n- [ ] Endpoint fuse opens only after three consecutive eligible exhausted logical outcomes across two tickets; provider fuse additionally requires two endpoint families; matching success resets state.\n- [ ] Physical attempts, recovered warnings, permanent failures, ticket-local 404s, and opaque diagnostics never increment inferred fuse counters.\n- [ ] Remaining matching work is explicitly deferred with reason/scope/`retry_not_before`; applied, failed, deferred, skipped, and recovered tallies plus exit status are exact.\n- [ ] Historical replay fixtures and verified-fake Cloud/DC batches show no premature termination of observed successful/partially successful work.","id":"28a3-a62d-6345-44a0","parent_id":"4217-d1d6-370b-4e98","priority":1,"tags":["rp03","reconciler","jira","reliability","tdd"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-03 S3 — Coordinate non-create operations with deferral and the scoped fuse"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787022577489555001,"uuid":"eb538b59-2b03-4364-bdd2-6cb769de0531"}